	(text "EoS ESP32 DevKit, rev A. Designed by Kartikeydheer Srivastava.\nCopyright (c) 2026 Kartikeydheer Srivastava. All rights reserved; see LICENSE.txt.\nValues from Espressif's ESP32-WROOM-32E datasheet v2.1 (sections 6 and 9) and ESP32 Hardware\nDesign Guidelines, the esptool docs (automatic bootloader), Silicon Labs CP2102N Rev. 1.5,\nDiodes AP7361C DS37274, onsemi MMBT3904, Nexperia PMEG6010CEH, Littelfuse SP0503BAHTG, Littelfuse 1206L, Kingbright.\nU1: KiCad's ESP32-WROOM-32E symbol; its stacked GND pin [1,15,38,39] is expanded to the four pads.\nR12 (5.1 kohm) bleeds D1's reverse leakage off VBUS, so a 5V-pin supply does not fake a USB host.\nGPIO6-11 are the module's internal flash pins and are not led out: J2 16-18, J3 17-19 are NC.\nHeader grid and pinout from Espressif's DevKitC V4 user guide (positions and names only)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
